  "notes": "Short for {自分撮|じぶんど}り (photographing oneself). A modern word that emerged with the spread of smartphones.\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed as a suru-verb: {自撮|じど}りする. The English loanword セルフィー is understood but {自撮|じど}り is the standard Japanese term.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自撮|じど}りする: to take a selfie\n- {自撮|じど}り{棒|ぼう}: selfie stick\n- {自撮|じど}り{写真|しゃしん}: selfie photo\n- {自撮|じど}りカメラ: front-facing camera\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nTaking selfies and posting them on SNS (social media) is very common in Japan. Some tourist spots and restaurants are known as popular {自撮|じど}りスポット (selfie spots). Note that {自撮|じど}り{棒|ぼう} are prohibited at many Japanese museums and train stations.",
